naccuracy","inaccuracy","best","best","inaccuracy","best","blunder","miss","best","best","best","good","best","best","best","best","best","best","brilliant","inaccuracy","great","best","inaccuracy","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","inaccuracy","great","blunder","miss","inaccuracy","good","best","inaccuracy","best","best","inaccuracy","miss","best","excellent","excellent","inaccuracy","mistake","great","best","great","good","blunder","great","best","best","inaccuracy","good","best","good","good","good","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","good","inaccuracy","good","excellent","excellent","good","best","good","good","good","best","best","best","good","best","best","best","forced","best","best","good","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","excellent","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","forced","excellent","best","best","best","best","inaccuracy","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best"],"moments":[{"ply":39,"name":"20.Nc3","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"20.Nc3!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Leaves the knight on d4 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 20…Bxd4 21.Nxd5 Bxf2+ 22.Qxf2 the engine rates it 0.00.","Attacks the d5 pawn, which is undefended.","20.Nc3 threatens Nxd5, winning a rook and a pawn, and stops …Rae8.","It threatens Nxd5, winning a rook and a pawn, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black was threatening …Rae8, winning a knight for a pawn, picking it up with 21…Bxb5. Nc3 takes care of it."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"20.Nc3!! leaves the knight on d4 hanging. Taking it gives White the material back and more."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"20.Nc3 leaves the knight on d4 hanging to the bishop on c5. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It threatens Nxd5, winning the queen and a pawn."},{"title":"If Black takes the knight","text":"20…Bxd4 is met by 21.Nxd5, taking the d5 pawn and threatening Nxb6, winning the queen for a knight. Then 22.Qxf2 takes the bishop on f2, and 23.Kxf2 takes the queen on f2. White ends up a piece ahead: White holds the balance (−0.03). This is Black's best try."}]},{"ply":41,"name":"21.Bxe5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"21.Bxe5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on e5.","Shores up the knight on d4, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1).","The next best move, 21.Red1, would drop White's winning chances from 55% to 40% (−1.13).","21.Bxe5 stops …Bxd4.","Black was threatening …Bxd4, winning a knight. Bxe5 takes care of it.","Trades bishop for knight."]},{"ply":51,"name":"26.b4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"26.b4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the knight on c5, which was hanging.","Takes c5 and a5 away from the Black queen on b6.","The next best move, 26.Nxd7, would drop White's winning chances from 59% to 28% (−2.54).","26.b4 protects the knight on c5 and takes c5 and a5 away from the queen.","Black answers 26…Qc7, aiming at the h2 pawn, a weak point next to the king, leaving White with a king with pawns missing from its shelter.","After 26…Qc7 27.f4 Re8 28.Qxc1 b6 29.Nxd7 d4, White comes out 6 points of material up (+0.59)."]},{"ply":52,"name":"26…a5","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"26…a5 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 45% to 16%.","points":["White answers 27.Nxd7, which takes the bishop on d7.","After Nxd7, White wins 6 points of material within 4 moves.","Better was 26…Qc7 (+0.59), which protects the bishop on d7, which was hanging."],"better":"26…Qc7 stops Nxd7. After 27.f4 Re8 28.Qxc1 b6 29.Nxd7 d4, Black is 6 points of material down (+0.59)."},{"ply":67,"name":"34.Ng3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"34.Ng3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 34.f3, would drop White's winning chances from 70% to 56% (+0.66).","34.Ng3 gets the knight out of the way of …Rxe4.","Black was threatening …Rxe4, winning a knight for a rook. The knight steps away.","The engine's plan continues with Nd3 and Qd1: this move is the first step.","Black answers 34…b6, attacking the knight on c5.","Engine line: 34…b6 35.Nd3 Re7 36.Qd1 Ra7 37.Qg4 (+2.42)."]},{"ply":69,"name":"35.Nd3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"35.Nd3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked knight to safety.","Attacks the rook on e5.","The next best move, 35.Nce4, would drop White's winning chances from 68% to 24% (−3.13).","35.Nd3 gets the knight out of the way of …bxc5 and threatens Nxe5, winning the exchange.","Black was threatening …bxc5, winning a knight. The knight steps away.","It threatens Nxe5, winning the exchange, so Black has to spend the next move on it."]},{"ply":71,"name":"36.Nf4","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"36.Nf4 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 74% to 10%.","points":["Black answers 36…Qc1+: the queen forks the king and the knight: both can't be saved at once.","After Qc1+, Black wins 3 points of material within 4 moves.","Better was 36.Qf7 (+2.89)."],"better":"36.Qf7 prepares Qh5 and Ne2. Engine line: 36…Qe6 37.Qh5 Rd8 38.Ne2 Kg8 39.Nef4 (+2.89)."},{"ply":72,"name":"36…Qc1+","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"36…Qc1+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen forks the king and the knight: both can't be saved at once.","The next best move, 36…Qd7, would drop Black's winning chances from 90% to 31% (+2.17).","36…Qc1+ wins a knight, picking it up with 37…Qxf4, and forks the king and the knight.","Sets up a sequence and wins a knight once the captures settle, picking it up with 37…Qxf4.","White answers 37.Kh2.","After 37.Kh2 Qxf4 38.Qf7 Rg8 39.Qd7 d3 40.Qxd3 Qxf2 41.Nh5, Black comes out a piece up (−5.70)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Bogo-Indian Defense: Retreat Variation","eco":"E11","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 5.Qc2: 9 moves in all, 5 by White and 4 by Black.","Theory runs out after 5.Qc2: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}